WEBVTT

00:02.270 --> 00:03.350
Huh?

00:03.350 --> 00:08.820
I think it's okay for at least one person to 
pick up what you're trying to throw away.

00:09.770 --> 00:11.030
So...

00:13.260 --> 00:16.490
Goodbye, Makabe Masamune-kun.

01:47.080 --> 01:53.050
<b>#11 "Face Your Feelings"</b>

01:47.990 --> 01:48.810
Hoshino.

01:48.810 --> 01:49.540
Here.

01:50.130 --> 01:50.960
Honjou.

01:50.960 --> 01:51.910
Here.

01:52.340 --> 01:53.230
Makabe.

01:55.940 --> 01:58.130
Makabe's absent again?

01:58.750 --> 02:00.530
Next, Mishima.

02:00.530 --> 02:01.450
Here.

02:01.450 --> 02:02.100
Mutou.

02:02.100 --> 02:03.010
Here.

02:03.620 --> 02:04.530
Yaguchi.

02:06.930 --> 02:10.020
Man, Masamune-kun's still absent.

02:10.340 --> 02:12.130
Is this three days now?

02:12.130 --> 02:13.930
Today is the fourth day.

02:13.930 --> 02:16.610
Spring break might start 
before he comes back.

02:18.890 --> 02:21.890
Fujinomiya-san, do you know anything?

02:21.890 --> 02:25.700
No... I'm terribly sorry, but I do not.

02:25.700 --> 02:29.200
I've sent him messages, 
but he hasn't responded.

02:29.200 --> 02:31.370
He's been ignoring you, too?

02:31.370 --> 02:33.880
Is he so sick that he 
can't even get out of bed?

02:33.880 --> 02:35.650
If his condition was that grave,

02:35.650 --> 02:39.240
I don't think our teacher would be 
calling his name every morning.

02:39.240 --> 02:40.630
True.

02:40.630 --> 02:44.210
Being absent without permission
for three or four days won't

02:44.210 --> 02:45.580
damage his record, will it?

02:45.580 --> 02:47.930
I'm not sure.

02:48.550 --> 02:50.940
Oh, it's Adagaki-san.

02:52.500 --> 02:53.930
Adagaki-san!

02:55.270 --> 02:56.510
Futaba-san.

02:57.100 --> 02:59.510
Thank goodness. Perfect timing.

03:00.360 --> 03:04.160
Hey, does Masamune-kun have, 
like, a cold or something?

03:04.160 --> 03:05.300
A cold?

03:05.300 --> 03:11.340
I mean, he's been absent for four days,
and he hasn't contacted any of us.

03:11.340 --> 03:14.590
Well, that sounds awful. 
I hope he's doing all right.

03:14.590 --> 03:17.900
Wait... Did you not know?

03:17.900 --> 03:20.020
I did not. This is the first I've heard of it.

03:20.020 --> 03:22.550
Huh?! B-But you two are dating, aren't you?

03:23.490 --> 03:26.310
No, we've broken up.

03:34.790 --> 03:37.100
What do you mean, Aki-sama?

03:37.100 --> 03:40.650
Exactly what it sounds like. 
I broke up with Makabe.

03:40.650 --> 03:43.110
No... But you can't do that!

03:43.530 --> 03:45.570
You can't, Aki-sama!

03:45.570 --> 03:50.300
I don't remember you getting 
to decide that for me, Yoshino.

03:51.690 --> 03:55.790
Anyway, it's over now. 
There's no point in discussing it further.

04:03.270 --> 04:06.630
You didn't know about those two, 
either, Koiwai-san?

04:07.230 --> 04:11.590
Not only did I not know... 
This is all a mistake.

04:11.990 --> 04:13.060
A mistake?

04:13.370 --> 04:17.480
After school, I'm going to Pig's Foot's— 
to Makabe-kun's house.

04:17.480 --> 04:19.920
To visit him? Then I'll go, too.

04:19.920 --> 04:21.280
M-Me, too!

04:21.690 --> 04:23.410
What about you, Fujinomiya-san?

04:25.170 --> 04:26.740
I'll also go.

04:26.740 --> 04:30.320
I think someone triggered 
something they shouldn't have.

04:30.320 --> 04:32.450
Um... Koiwai-san?

04:32.450 --> 04:35.710
But if I can find out the reason, 
I'll know how to follow through.

04:38.890 --> 04:40.130
Huh...

04:40.530 --> 04:43.720
So this is what Masamune-kun's 
house looks like.

04:43.720 --> 04:46.090
I-It's pretty nice.

04:46.500 --> 04:50.970
I believe that Koiwai-san 
and myself have visited before.

04:50.970 --> 04:52.740
What? Really?

04:52.740 --> 04:55.090
It was incredibly awkward.

04:55.090 --> 04:56.560
What do you mean?

04:56.950 --> 04:58.980
I guess now's not the time for that.

05:05.380 --> 05:06.620
Is no one home?

05:06.620 --> 05:09.490
Now that you mention it, 
I don't see any lights on.

05:09.490 --> 05:10.860
What?

05:10.860 --> 05:13.180
What should we do with these puddings?

05:13.180 --> 05:15.460
They're super fluffy ones, 
made with eggs from the highlands.

05:15.460 --> 05:17.920
<i>Pudding?</i>

05:18.650 --> 05:19.900
Chinatsu-chan?

05:26.380 --> 05:29.310
I smell pudding!

05:36.050 --> 05:39.810
Yeah... Humans definitely 
can't live on just school meals.

05:39.810 --> 05:42.970
Thanks for the treat. 
They were super delicious!

05:42.970 --> 05:47.120
W-Were they? They're puddings from 
a pâtisserie that's all the rage right now.

05:47.120 --> 05:49.310
Are you my brother's friends?

05:49.710 --> 05:52.810
Yet you're this keen on sweets?

05:53.460 --> 05:55.270
Th-Thanks?

05:58.730 --> 06:03.160
Pardon my asking, but has 
something happened at home?

06:03.160 --> 06:07.950
Well, my mom's been sorta, uh...

06:14.660 --> 06:15.770
What's in there?

06:15.770 --> 06:17.340
My brother's room.

06:21.860 --> 06:24.980
Oh, sorry. I've been a bit busy.

06:26.620 --> 06:29.030
Mom? I'm coming in.

06:34.610 --> 06:36.450
Whoa. All this stuff to get swole.

06:36.450 --> 06:38.910
I guess that's not surprising 
coming from Masamune-sama.

06:39.970 --> 06:44.610
Mom, Onii-chan's friends are here to visit.

06:46.010 --> 06:49.340
Maa-kun? Is that you, Maa-kun?

06:49.740 --> 06:53.050
No, they're Onii-chan's friends.

06:53.050 --> 06:55.170
They brought pudding, too. Do you want some?

06:55.550 --> 06:58.460
No... Maa-kun...

06:58.460 --> 07:02.520
Why did you disappear, Maa-kun?

07:02.520 --> 07:03.420
Gyof.

07:04.470 --> 07:07.820
Waaah! Maa-kun!

07:07.820 --> 07:10.260
Why did you leave me?!

07:08.900 --> 07:11.650
Leave? What does she mean?

07:11.650 --> 07:17.070
My brother ended up going to our grandpa's 
place in Shinshu, and he took all his stuff.

07:17.450 --> 07:18.540
What?!

07:18.540 --> 07:20.180
Shinshu?

07:20.720 --> 07:22.290
I guess it wasn't a cold.

07:22.970 --> 07:26.020
He went out last weekend,
and when he came back,

07:26.020 --> 07:28.320
he suddenly wouldn't listen to us.

07:28.320 --> 07:32.700
But I tried! I tried to stop him!

07:32.700 --> 07:34.010
Yes, yes.

07:34.520 --> 07:35.650
As you can see,

07:35.650 --> 07:39.690
Mom's not functioning as a person anymore,
and the chores are just piling up.

07:39.690 --> 07:41.540
I have no idea what's going on.

07:42.190 --> 07:43.730
Last weekend...

07:44.160 --> 07:45.440
Any ideas?

07:45.440 --> 07:48.280
He went on a date with Aki-sama.

07:48.280 --> 07:50.410
Do you think something happened then?

07:50.920 --> 07:52.960
That sounds quite likely.

07:52.960 --> 07:56.800
Maybe Adagaki-san gave him a 
really mean nickname or something.

07:56.800 --> 07:58.660
And he decided to run away?

07:59.670 --> 08:03.620
We have no way of getting 
through to my brother.

08:04.170 --> 08:08.800
Whether he comes or goes, 
he won't listen to what we have to say.

08:09.210 --> 08:12.810
Even though he has all these people 
worrying about him now...

08:14.310 --> 08:17.150
My brother really is an idiot.

08:18.560 --> 08:20.930
I'm sorry about this, 
after you came to visit...

08:20.930 --> 08:23.840
No, no. I'm sorry we dropped by out of the blue.

08:23.840 --> 08:27.340
It's fine. I think my mom 
regained some of her sanity.

08:28.400 --> 08:33.210
We can't get a hold of him, 
but if we hear anything, we'll contact you.

08:33.210 --> 08:34.360
Thanks!

08:34.360 --> 08:36.220
We look forward to hearing from you.

08:39.330 --> 08:41.500
Well, that didn't really get us anywhere.

08:41.940 --> 08:47.300
But at least we know where he is now, 
even if all we can do is wait.

08:47.700 --> 08:50.340
I think waiting for him is important, too.

08:50.600 --> 08:52.670
Yeah, you're right.

08:54.250 --> 08:55.250
I'll see you later.

09:02.990 --> 09:04.890
Wait for him, huh?

09:04.890 --> 09:06.620
Indeed.

09:06.620 --> 09:10.380
But, man... Shinshu? That's so far.

09:10.380 --> 09:13.620
It certainly doesn't change 
the fact that we're worried.

09:14.470 --> 09:16.740
What do you mean by that, exactly?

09:17.270 --> 09:19.260
What are <i>you</i> worried about?

09:19.260 --> 09:20.990
You're actually happy, aren't you?

09:20.990 --> 09:22.300
Koiwai-san?

09:23.190 --> 09:26.230
This is all your fault to begin with.

09:26.920 --> 09:30.620
You got into Aki-sama's head, and now 
you got exactly what you wanted.

09:30.620 --> 09:31.300
Hey!

09:31.300 --> 09:33.720
You went out of your way to 
do something so underhanded...

09:33.720 --> 09:37.650
Even though Pig's Foot is never 
going to look your way anyway.

09:42.210 --> 09:47.450
In that case, wouldn't you say what 
you've been doing is also rather deceitful?

09:47.450 --> 09:48.350
Deceitful?

09:48.350 --> 09:52.800
You've known where Masamune-sama's 
feelings lay for a long time.

09:52.800 --> 09:55.440
And yet, you ignored them 
and sent Aki-sama after him.

09:55.440 --> 09:58.930
Just to protect yourself, 
you lied about your own feelings!

09:58.930 --> 10:00.990
My feelings don't matter here!

10:00.990 --> 10:03.170
If this ain't deceit, then what is it?!

10:03.170 --> 10:05.060
You're the biggest coward here!

10:05.060 --> 10:08.710
Who cares about your past 
or Adagaki-san's past?!

10:09.620 --> 10:14.170
I have nothing! I have absolutely nothing!

10:19.230 --> 10:20.410
That's enough.

10:21.830 --> 10:25.790
Stop fighting out here. 
You'll bother the neighbors.

10:26.530 --> 10:31.050
Futaba-san, I'm sorry, but could 
you walk Fujinomiya-san home?

10:31.050 --> 10:32.150
Sure.

10:51.210 --> 10:53.710
Let's have a chat.

10:54.460 --> 10:57.410
Just the two of us. One on one.

11:14.060 --> 11:15.480
I think that should do it.

11:20.690 --> 11:22.950
Oh, look at those flames go.

11:24.300 --> 11:28.250
<i>It's not like staring at a bonfire 
is gonna give me any answers...</i>

11:28.250 --> 11:31.350
<i>But I really don't want to think 
about anything right now.</i>

11:32.170 --> 11:36.780
<i>I came here when I felt like this as a kid, too.</i>

11:37.770 --> 11:42.560
<i>But this time, I have no one to hate.</i>

11:42.560 --> 11:43.790
<i>So why...</i>

11:45.090 --> 11:46.330
Masamune.

11:47.860 --> 11:49.070
Grandfather.

11:50.670 --> 11:52.310
What's this?

11:52.850 --> 11:56.930
You're not allowed to bring 
snacks into this household.

11:58.500 --> 12:02.070
I'm terribly sorry. I wasn't thinking.

12:11.470 --> 12:15.910
I guess burning them doesn't even 
create a sweet scent or anything...

12:28.580 --> 12:33.640
Thinking back on everything, I don't think 
we've ever had a proper conversation.

12:34.270 --> 12:38.500
Not putting aside that I'm the daughter of 
the Adagaki family, and you're the daughter

12:38.500 --> 12:40.110
of the Koiwai family who serves us.

12:41.020 --> 12:45.570
Can we actually put aside 
status and talk, though?

12:45.990 --> 12:50.890
I think I thought the same thing, which is 
why I never properly acknowledged you.

12:51.610 --> 12:54.180
Even though you've been 
right by my side this whole time.

12:56.220 --> 12:57.900
We've done so much together.

12:58.390 --> 12:59.500
We have.

12:59.930 --> 13:01.960
And you've done a lot for me.

13:01.960 --> 13:03.270
I have...

13:04.410 --> 13:05.680
A lot.

13:12.290 --> 13:16.030
<i>I wonder what kind of memories 
Aki-sama is remembering.</i>

13:17.260 --> 13:19.530
But this is my job.

13:19.960 --> 13:23.610
It's because I've always relied on you so much

13:23.610 --> 13:27.060
that your only choice was to 
kill off your own feelings...

13:27.550 --> 13:29.700
Even though you like Makabe.

13:34.900 --> 13:37.080
You couldn't say that even if you wanted to.

13:37.820 --> 13:42.050
N-No... No, no, no, you're wro—

13:44.370 --> 13:46.050
I'm sorry, Yoshino.

13:46.460 --> 13:47.980
Aki-sama...

13:47.980 --> 13:50.850
It must've been really hard this whole time.

13:54.190 --> 13:55.430
Do you like him?

13:59.910 --> 14:03.770
I just want you to be happy, Aki-sama...

14:04.650 --> 14:07.320
Well, that's something for me to decide.

14:07.320 --> 14:09.790
You don't need to worry about that.

14:11.270 --> 14:13.670
But this is what I decided deep down.

14:13.980 --> 14:17.780
I did something awful that 
could never be forgiven, so...

14:17.780 --> 14:20.080
I need to make up for it, at least a little.

14:21.610 --> 14:24.300
But when I spent more time with him...

14:22.840 --> 14:24.800
<b>Contacts</b>

14:22.840 --> 14:24.800
<b>Pig's Foot</b>

14:25.370 --> 14:26.760
I just...

14:31.090 --> 14:33.860
I'm sorry, Aki-sama!

14:33.860 --> 14:38.390
I understand how you feel. 
So don't apologize.

14:39.990 --> 14:44.140
This will be the last time 
I request something from you.

14:44.700 --> 14:47.450
I want you to properly face your own feelings.

14:49.180 --> 14:52.570
Go. Tell him how you feel yourself.

14:58.530 --> 15:00.540
Okay, Aki-sama.

15:05.470 --> 15:09.300
The next time we see each other, 
you can just call me "Aki"!

15:23.810 --> 15:32.780
<b>Karaoke</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Vocal Volume</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Stability</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Technique</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Enthusiasm</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Rhythm</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<i><b>Points</b></i>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Comments:</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
You are a very talented singer!

You're definitely the honor student type.

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Calories burned:</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Stop Song    to stop              Previous                 Next                  to choose</b>

15:32.780 --> 15:35.740
<b>Preview            Next</b>

15:35.740 --> 15:38.250
You set a new record!

15:38.250 --> 15:39.650
I'm honored.

15:40.130 --> 15:42.710
Now, let's order more drinks!

15:43.460 --> 15:47.270
Futaba-san, thank you for being so considerate.

15:47.270 --> 15:49.300
What are you talking about?

15:50.070 --> 15:54.010
The only ways to heal a broken heart 
are overeating and karaoke!

15:54.010 --> 15:55.850
That's common knowledge for girls!

15:56.450 --> 15:57.510
Common knowledge...

15:58.190 --> 16:01.450
Well, I do think I feel a little better.

16:01.450 --> 16:04.960
You know, it wouldn't hurt to 
look around you a bit more.

16:04.960 --> 16:06.830
What do you mean?

16:07.710 --> 16:10.070
For example, other classmates...

16:10.480 --> 16:12.240
Like, what about Kojuurou-kyun?

16:13.530 --> 16:18.080
Masamune x Kojuurou,
a.k.a. MasaKoju, is my ship,

16:18.080 --> 16:21.060
but I wouldn't mind sharing him with you.

16:21.670 --> 16:24.460
I can't say I feel anything right now...

16:24.460 --> 16:27.780
I see. I mean, I guess you did love him.

16:29.430 --> 16:31.220
Say, Fujinomiya-san.

16:31.220 --> 16:34.930
If you truly fall in love, there's something 
that will always remain with you.

16:35.410 --> 16:37.430
No girl is truly empty inside.

16:39.750 --> 16:42.390
Thank you very much, Futaba-san.

16:42.970 --> 16:46.860
Okay! We should sing this next song together!

16:46.860 --> 16:49.690
Oh, then maybe we should 
sing the <i>Hada Pure</i> song.

16:49.690 --> 16:51.170
Okay!

16:51.610 --> 16:55.610
Let's see... Okay, sent!

16:56.780 --> 16:58.460
H-Huh?

16:58.460 --> 16:59.330
That's not it?

16:59.330 --> 17:00.580
What song is this?

17:09.490 --> 17:12.210
Hey... Let me through.

17:14.220 --> 17:16.220
<b>Chinatsu
My grandpa's address is Otari,
Nagano Prefecture...</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Hakutaka</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Kanazawa</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>12 cars</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Kagayaki</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Kanazawa</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>10 cars</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Asama</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Nagano</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>12 cars</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Hakutaka</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Kanazawa</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>12 cars</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Asama</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Nagano</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>12 cars</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Kagayaki</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>Kanazawa</b>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.600
<b>10 cars</b>

17:48.300 --> 17:52.590
<i>I'm such a shameless liar.</i>

17:55.910 --> 17:57.620
Look at him!

17:57.620 --> 18:00.660
Isn't Makabe Masamune-kun handsome?

18:02.800 --> 18:07.270
<i>When we reunited in high school, 
I felt like my breathing might stop.</i>

18:07.650 --> 18:10.320
<i>I decided to see how things 
would go before setting a trap,</i>

18:10.320 --> 18:12.190
<i>and the hot guy easily fell for it.</i>

18:13.060 --> 18:14.650
<i>He's such a simpleton.</i>

18:15.350 --> 18:18.360
I still have no regrets about 
trying to give that woman

18:18.360 --> 18:20.630
a taste of her own medicine.

18:20.630 --> 18:22.490
<i>And so stubborn at the most awkward times.</i>

18:23.510 --> 18:26.210
Don't get caught up in her pace.

18:26.210 --> 18:27.760
That's not happening.

18:28.380 --> 18:30.880
<i>He doesn't make any sense and he's oblivious.</i>

18:32.770 --> 18:33.840
<i>So...</i>

18:34.770 --> 18:38.230
<i>I never thought my heart would hurt.</i>

18:39.150 --> 18:41.730
<i>I tried to pretend I didn't notice it.</i>

18:41.730 --> 18:43.210
<i>I thought I could.</i>

18:43.890 --> 18:45.010
<i>But...</i>

18:45.010 --> 18:49.940
I think I had the most fun when 
I was devising my plan with you.

18:50.490 --> 18:51.980
<i>There was no way I could tell him...</i>

18:53.220 --> 18:55.370
<i>that I had fun, too.</i>

18:57.650 --> 19:01.550
<i>Even so, Aki-sama told me to move forward.</i>

19:10.290 --> 19:12.650
I'm getting off. Please let me through.

19:14.830 --> 19:16.800
Man, this fog is dense.

19:18.490 --> 19:20.390
I guess I'll clean up the firewood.

19:38.730 --> 19:42.460
Gwandfather... I can't run anymo—

19:44.290 --> 19:45.370
<i>That's...</i>

19:50.770 --> 19:52.130
Hey, Little Me.

19:52.130 --> 19:53.420
Hey, Big Me.

19:53.420 --> 19:56.620
Diet and exercise are pretty rough, huh? 
Why not run away?

19:56.620 --> 19:59.140
N-No! I can't!

19:59.140 --> 20:00.100
Why's that?

20:01.170 --> 20:02.760
Because I'm gonna get revenge!

20:06.660 --> 20:08.300
Revenge, huh?

20:08.300 --> 20:10.560
That's right! Revenge!

20:10.560 --> 20:13.210
I'm gonna get my revenge and make her pay!

20:13.210 --> 20:14.850
That's why I won't run away!

20:17.500 --> 20:19.280
Listen, Little Me.

20:20.170 --> 20:22.220
She's not your enemy.

20:22.830 --> 20:24.600
The enemy's already been defeated.

20:24.600 --> 20:25.270
Huh?

20:25.770 --> 20:28.010
I'm sure that just sounds like 
some pleasantries...

20:28.430 --> 20:32.730
But right now, there are no enemies 
in front of me. Not a single one.

20:33.660 --> 20:36.290
So... you don't have to worry.

20:37.330 --> 20:40.140
All your hard work won't go to waste, either.

20:40.660 --> 20:43.300
It might not be exactly how you imagined it...

20:44.610 --> 20:47.850
But you and I will be okay.

20:50.220 --> 20:53.580
<i>Because we just had the 
wrong idea about something.</i>

